<%# Top of a closed tender's page, where most search visitors arrive (most
    land on tenders that closed long ago): what to do next. locals: tender,
    open_similar (count of open similar tenders), result (:winner when the
    bid result names one, :details for other result data, else nil) %>
<div class="mb-6 rounded-lg border border-amber-200 bg-amber-50 p-4 sm:p-5 dark:border-amber-800 dark:bg-amber-950">
  <p class="text-sm font-semibold text-amber-900 dark:text-amber-100">
    This tender closed on <%= tender.submission_close_date.strftime('%d %b %Y') %>.
    <% if open_similar.positive? %>
      <%= pluralize(open_similar, 'tender') %> like it <%= open_similar == 1 ? 'is' : 'are' %> open now.
    <% end %>
  </p>
  <div class="mt-3 flex flex-wrap gap-2">
    <% if open_similar.positive? %>
      <a href="#similar-tenders" class="rounded-md bg-orange-600 px-3 py-2 text-sm font-semibold text-white hover:bg-orange-700">See open tenders like this</a>
    <% end %>
    <a href="#relevant_tenders_form" class="rounded-md border border-orange-600 bg-white px-3 py-2 text-sm font-semibold text-orange-700 hover:bg-orange-50 dark:bg-transparent">Get alerts for new ones</a>
    <% if result %>
      <a href="#bid-results" class="rounded-md border border-emerald-300 bg-white px-3 py-2 text-sm font-semibold text-emerald-800 hover:bg-emerald-50 dark:bg-transparent dark:text-emerald-300"><%= result == :winner ? 'See who won' : 'See the bid result' %></a>
    <% end %>
  </div>
</div>
